From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] EDEN_UP_DRIVER_BUILD_LOG=1: driver pipeline build times and GPU-thread compute translation counts (log only)

Port of Eglantine-Community 212568b2 ("video_core: log driver pipeline build times", handle
kraibse). Off by default; with the switch unset every changed site makes the same driver call
and nothing else.

Every 10 s with builds: how many graphics and compute pipelines the driver built, how many took
over 10 ms (compiled, not taken from the driver's cache), mean and maximum. The task, scan and
mesh compute pipelines of EDEN_NX2_MESH_AS_COMPUTE count as compute; with
EDEN_NX2_RADV_MESH_COMPUTE (the console) a mesh pipeline is one graphics build, the driver's
compute lowering inside it. Builds made before the first
frame (the boot) come out as the first line, with the time since the first of them as its window;
that stands in for upstream's "at boot" summary, which is not ported.

Ours, for the warm-compute decision: every 5 s with any, how many compute pipelines and how many
mesh pipelines were translated with the runtime pools (main_pools: the GPU thread). A mesh
pipeline counts whether the driver (EDEN_NX2_RADV_MESH_COMPUTE, what the console runs) or the
core (EDEN_NX2_MESH_AS_COMPUTE) runs it as compute. Kept translations (EDEN_UP_SHADER_PREP),
stage cache hits and worker translations (EDEN_UP_ASYNC_TRANSLATION) are not counted: nothing is
translated on the GPU thread for them. A window with none is not logged.

Builder threads only add to the window under the lock and never log; the frame's thread
(PipelineCache::TickFrame) takes the due windows and logs after the lock is released, so a
builder that waits for heap memory (EDEN_UP_HEAP_WAIT_MS) never holds a lock the frame needs.

v2 of draft-d-pipeline-build-log.patch (review of 2026-11-10): the mesh count no longer needs
EDEN_NX2_MESH_AS_COMPUTE (it was always 0 on the console) and counts translations, not
attempts; no log call under the lock or on a builder thread; one line when the switch is read;
empty windows not logged; the mean's division cast for -Wconversion.

Test: env.txt EDEN_UP_DRIVER_BUILD_LOG=1, cold then warm driver cache, the door walk. grep
"EDEN_UP_DRIVER_BUILD_LOG on", "Driver pipeline builds", "GPU thread compute translations".
Not compiled for the console; the header alone was syntax-checked on the host (clang++
-std=c++20 -Wall -Wextra -Wconversion, no warnings).

